================================================================================
env.summary - Stage7 environment variables by consuming service
================================================================================

Generated from the current source tree. Every entry below is read via
process.env in non-test service code (services/*/src, shared-nextgen/src).

Scope notes
-----------
* docker-compose.yaml mounts the whole .env into every container through
  "env_file". The sections here describe what each service READS, not what it
  receives. A variable can therefore be visible to a service it does not use.
* Values shown are the .env.example defaults or placeholders. Never put a real
  secret in this file; it is committed.
* Entries come from three places: direct process.env reads in non-test source,
  computed reads (process.env[persistenceEnvVar], process.env[`${prefix}_...`]),
  and the compose file itself. A variable marked [not in .env.example] has a
  built-in default in code and is not part of the shipped .env template.
* .env is read by Docker Compose at build time too. worker-pool takes
  STAGE7_ASSISTANTS as a build arg and prunes unselected assistant folders from
  the image, so changing it requires a rebuild of that image.

Variables in .env.example that no code reads
--------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_URL, ANTHROPIC_MESSAGES_PATH, OLLAMA_PROXY_BASE, and the four
CAREER_* budget variables are documented in .env.example but are not read
anywhere. Provider endpoints for Gemini and Anthropic are hardcoded in their
provider classes. NODE_ENV and NODE_OPTIONS are not read by application code
either, but they are consumed by the Node runtime and the frontend build, so
they still have an effect.

Variables read by code that .env.example omits
-----------------------------------------------
Most of them. The template documents the infrastructure and the LLM providers,
but not the per-assistant persistence variables, the tool-executor store and
skill endpoint variables, VAULT_URL, AGENT_RUNTIME_URL, TOOL_EXECUTOR_URL,
ADMIN_*, or ARTIFACTS_S3_*. All of them have defaults, so an incomplete
.env still boots.

Formerly documented variables that no longer exist anywhere in the code (the
v6 topology they belonged to): CLIENT_SECRET, SHARED_SECRET, ADMIN_SECRET,
JWT_SECRET, JWT_REFRESH_SECRET, GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_USERNAME,
GIT_REPOSITORY_URL, GIT_DEFAULT_BRANCH, GITHUB_EMAIL, POSTOFFICE_URL,
LIBRARIAN_URL, and all per-service *_SECRET values.

================================================================================
/infrastructure - mongo, redis (docker-compose.yaml)
================================================================================

Neither container has an env_file, and neither service reads process.env.
They are configured entirely in docker-compose.yaml.

No environment variables.

================================================================================
/shared-nextgen
================================================================================

SERVICE_NAME=stage7
  Log source label for the shared pino logger. Default: nextgen.

================================================================================
/services/gateway  (host 3900, container 3000)
================================================================================

PORT=3000
  Container listen port. Default: 3000.

WORKER_POOL_URL=http://worker-pool:3200
  Backend used by the /api/workers routes. Default: http://worker-pool:3200.

SERVICE_NAME=stage7
  Via shared-nextgen logger.

Gateway routes for the other services use hard-coded container URLs
(brain:3100, worker-pool:3200, mcp-runtime:3300, agent-runtime:3400,
tool-executor:3500, temporal:4100, vault:4000, artifacts:4200,
auth:4300). Those are not configurable through the environment; change them
in services/gateway/src/index.ts.

================================================================================
/services/brain  (host 3100, container 3100)
================================================================================

PORT=3100

-- Connection ------------------------------------------------------------------

REDIS_HOST=redis
REDIS_PORT=6379
  Semantic cache backend.

ARTIFACTS_URL=http://artifacts:4200
  Persistence for skill collections. Falls back to PERSISTENCE_URL, then to
  http://artifacts:4200.

PERSISTENCE_URL=  [not in .env.example]
  Legacy alias consulted when ARTIFACTS_URL is unset.

-- LLM providers ---------------------------------------------------------------

brain registers a provider only when its credential is present, so an unset
key means that provider is absent from the router rather than failing calls.

OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_BASE=  [not in .env.example, default https://api.openai.com/v1]
OPENAI_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
OPENAI_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
OPENAI_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

GROK_API_KEY=
XAI_API_KEY=  [not in .env.example]
  Either key enables the Grok provider.
GROK_API_BASE=  [not in .env.example, default https://api.x.ai/v1]
GROK_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
GROK_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
GROK_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

MISTRAL_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_BASE=  [not in .env.example, default https://api.mistral.ai/v1]
MISTRAL_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
MISTRAL_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
MISTRAL_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

GEMINI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=  [not in .env.example]
  Either key enables Gemini. The endpoint is hardcoded to
  https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com in the provider; there is no
  URL variable.

HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY=
HF_TOKEN=  [not in .env.example]
  Either credential enables Hugging Face.
HUGGINGFACE_API_BASE=  [not in .env.example, default https://router.huggingface.co/v1]
HUGGINGFACE_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
HUGGINGFACE_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
HUGGINGFACE_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
OPENROUTER_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
OPENROUTER_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
OPENROUTER_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
  Endpoint is hardcoded to https://api.anthropic.com in the provider.

OPENWEB_URL=
OPENWEBUI_URL=  [not in .env.example]
  Either base URL enables the OpenWebUI provider. A trailing /v1 is stripped.
OPENWEBUI_API_KEY=
OPENWEB_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/api/models
OPENWEB_CHAT_PATH=/api/chat/completions
OPENWEB_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions
OPENWEBUI_LIST_MODELS_PATH=  [not in .env.example, default /models]
OPENWEBUI_CHAT_PATH=  [not in .env.example, default /chat/completions]
OPENWEBUI_COMPLETIONS_PATH=  [not in .env.example, default /completions]
  The OPENWEB_* path variables are checked first, then the OPENWEBUI_* ones.

OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434/v1
OLLAMA_URL=  [not in .env.example]
  Either base enables Ollama; a missing /v1 suffix is appended.
OLLAMA_API_KEY=
OLLAMA_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
OLLAMA_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
OLLAMA_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_ACCOUNT_ID=

CUSTOM_PROVIDERS=
  Comma-separated third-party provider prefixes, e.g. REQUESTY,LLM7. Each
  prefix P requires P_API_KEY, P_API_NAME, and P_API_URL to be OpenAI
  compatible, and may set P_LIST_MODELS_PATH. Example set:
  REQUESTY_API_KEY, REQUESTY_API_NAME, REQUESTY_API_URL.

-- Timeouts and circuit breaker ------------------------------------------------

BRAIN_PROVIDER_TIMEOUT_MS=  [not in .env.example]
  Whole-request ceiling for a provider call. Default: provider-specific.

BRAIN_PROVIDER_ATTEMPT_TIMEOUT_MS=  [not in .env.example]
  Single attempt ceiling inside one call. Default: provider-specific.

BRAIN_COMPLETION_DEADLINE_MS=  [not in .env.example]
  Deadline for a completion. Default: derived from the timeout above.

BRAIN_CIRCUIT_THRESHOLD=  [not in .env.example]
  Consecutive provider failures before the circuit opens. Default: 8.

BRAIN_CIRCUIT_COOLDOWN_MS=  [not in .env.example]
  How long the circuit stays open. Default: 60000.

================================================================================
/services/worker-pool  (host 3200, container 3200)
================================================================================

PORT=3200

STAGE7_ASSISTANTS=
  Comma-separated assistant IDs to load. Empty means all 21. Also passed as
  the image build arg, which prunes the other assistant folders out of the
  image. An unknown ID fails the build (image) or refuses to boot (runtime).
  Valid IDs are the folder names under services/worker-pool/assistants/:
  analytics, career, content, cto, education, event, executive, finance,
  healthcare, hotel, hr, investment, legal, marketing, product, restaurant,
  sales, scriptwriter, songwriter, sports, support. The -canonical-assistant
  suffix is accepted and stripped.

REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379
  Task queue and cache.

MONGO_URI=mongodb://mongo:27017
MONGO_DB=stage7
  Read indirectly: worker-pool builds its persistence layer from
  ArtifactsService, which is the artifacts workspace library
  (@stage7-nextgen/artifacts). When MONGO_URI is set but Mongo is
  unreachable, this service refuses to start instead of falling back to a
  volatile in-memory store, and logs that MONGO_URI is not set when it is
  absent.

BRAIN_URL=http://brain:3100
TOOL_EXECUTOR_URL=  [not in .env.example, default http://tool-executor:3500]
  Downstream services used by assistant runtimes.

