================================================================================
/services/tool-executor  (host 3500, container 3500)
================================================================================

PORT=3500

-- Downstream services ---------------------------------------------------------

ARTIFACTS_URL=http://artifacts:4200
BRAIN_URL=http://brain:3100
WORKER_POOL_URL=http://worker-pool:3200
  Downstream bases for skills and reasoning delegation. BRAIN_URL must stay
  set: a skill that falls back to a direct brain call skips the call entirely
  when it is empty.

PERSISTENCE_URL=  [not in .env.example]
AGENT_RUNTIME_URL=  [not in .env.example]
  Also read as base-origin candidates for outbound HTTP: after a skill URL
  fails, tool-executor retries the same path against each of ARTIFACTS_URL,
  PERSISTENCE_URL, BRAIN_URL, WORKER_POOL_URL, and AGENT_RUNTIME_URL in turn
  before giving up.

VAULT_URL=  [not in .env.example, default http://vault:4000]
  Secret decryption endpoint used by the credential provider and CodeExecutor.

BRAIN_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
  Per-request ceiling for a reasoning call. Keep this under the gateway's
  60s proxy read timeout on /api.

BRAIN_FALLBACK_PROVIDER=  [not in .env.example]
BRAIN_FALLBACK_MODEL=  [not in .env.example]
  Used when a skill falls back to a direct brain call.

-- Assistant persistence homes -------------------------------------------------

Each assistant domain persists through its own Mongo-backed collection on the
artifacts service. The name is derived from the variable: HOTEL_HOME -> hotel,
LEGAL_HOME -> legal, STORAGE_DIR -> default. A skill that sets
persistenceEnvVar with no matching variable falls back to the "default"
collection, so an unset HOME silently merges a domain into shared storage.

STORAGE_DIR=  [not in .env.example]
  The default collection, used by any skill that declares no persistenceEnvVar.
  With no directory set at all, the inter-skill collection store falls back to
  the local temp path /tmp/stage7-store, which does not survive a restart.

ANALYTICS_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
CAREER_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
CONTENT_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
CTO_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
EDUCATION_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
EVENT_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
EXECUTIVE_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
FINANCE_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
HEALTHCARE_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
HOTEL_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
HR_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
INVESTMENT_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
LEGAL_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
MARKETING_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
PRODUCT_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
SALES_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
SCRIPTWRITING_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
SONGWRITING_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
SPORTS_GROUP_A_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
SPORTS_GROUP_B_HOME=  [not in .env.example]
SUPPORT_HOME=  [not in .env.example]

Two names that look like they belong here but are not read by any skill:

SPORTS_HOME, RESTAURANT_HOME
  Sports persists through SPORTS_GROUP_A_HOME and SPORTS_GROUP_B_HOME, and
  every restaurant skill declares STORAGE_DIR, so restaurant records land in
  the default collection. RESTAURANT_HOME appears only inside a skill
  description string. Setting either variable has no effect.

Every variable above is a "not in .env.example" entry: a skill that declares one
and finds it unset falls back to /var/data/stage7/<variable name, lowercased>,
for example /var/data/stage7/hotel_home for HOTEL_HOME. The deployment values
in .env use the shorter /var/data/stage7/hotel form, which only works because
those variables are set explicitly.

